      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I need to figure out the answer to this logical reasoning problem. Let me read through the context and the question again to make sure I understand it correctly.\n\nThe context says that a lot of people spit everywhere without any hesitation or guilt because the previous punishment measures aren't effective enough. It mentions that these punishments don't serve as a warning and don't reach the core of the spitters' hearts. Also, the spitters don't feel ashamed when they spit, and even after being punished, they still don't feel any shame.\n\nThe question is asking which option the author thinks is the best way to punish people who spit everywhere. The options are A, B, C, or D.\n\nLet me break this down. The context is talking about why current punishments aren't working. It says the punishments aren't a warning and don't touch the heart of the spitters. So, the author is pointing out that the current methods aren't effective because they don't address the underlying issue\u2014the lack of shame or guilt in the spitters.\n\nLooking at the options:\n\nA) We should give them proper guidance.\nB) Touch the depths of their heart.\nC) Not specified.\nD) We need to specify the punishment measures.\n\nHmm. The context mentions that the previous punishment measures are not enough because they don't touch the heart. So, the author is suggesting that the problem is that the punishments don't reach the spitters' hearts, meaning they don't make them feel ashamed or guilty. Therefore, the solution should involve touching their hearts.\n\nOption B says \"Touch the depths of their heart,\" which seems to align with what the context is saying. The author is implying that the current punishments don't do this, so the best way would be to implement punishments that do touch their hearts.\n\nOption A is about giving guidance, which might be related but the context specifically talks about punishment measures, not just guidance. Option D suggests specifying the punishment measures, but the context says the previous measures were not effective because they didn't touch the heart, so just specifying them might not solve the problem. Option C is \"Not specified,\" which doesn't seem right because the context does suggest a direction.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the author thinks that the best way is to touch the depths of their heart, which is option B.\n</think>\n\nThe author suggests that the best way to address the issue of spitting is by touching the depths of the spitters' hearts, as current punishments fail to instill a sense of shame. \n\nAnswer: B) Touch the depths of their heart.",
