 the second year?\n\nG must have been on the first year's committee. The first year's committee was H, F, V, Z. G wasn't on the first year's committee, so G can't be the chairman in the second year. So, B is invalid.\n\nOption C is Y. Y wasn't on the first year's committee because H was present, so Y can't be the chairman in the second year. So, C is invalid.\n\nOption D is I. I wasn't on the first year's committee because in the first year, the judges were H and F, and I was excluded. So, I wasn't on the first year's committee, so I can't be the chairman in the second year. So, D is invalid.\n\nTherefore, the only possible chairman in the second year is F, which is option A.\n\nWait, but let me double-check. In the second year, if F is the chairman, then the committee is F, I, Y, Z. That works.\n\nAlternatively, could the second year's committee have G as a judge? Let's see.\n\nIf in the second year, the judges are F and G, then the scientists must be two from V, Y, Z, but considering the constraints.\n\nBut if G is a judge, then V can't be a scientist because G and V can't be on the committee in the same year.\n\nSo, scientists must be Y and Z.\n\nSo, second year's committee:\n\nJudges: F, G\n\nScientists: Y, Z\n\nChairman: F\n\nThis also works.\n\nBut the chairman is F, so that's still option A.\n\nAlternatively, could the chairman be I? But I wasn't on the first year's committee, so no.\n\nWait, but in the second year, if I is a judge, then V can't be a scientist. So, scientists would be Y and Z.\n\nSo, the committee would be F, I, Y, Z, with chairman F.\n\nAlternatively, could the chairman be V? But V wasn't on the first year's committee as a scientist, but wait, V was on the first year's committee as a scientist. So, V could be the chairman in the second year.\n\nWait, but the options don't include V. The options are F, G, Y, I. So, V isn't an option, so even if V could be chairman, it's not among the choices.\n\nSimilarly, Z wasn't an option either.\n\nSo, the only possible chairman among the options is F.\n\nWait, but let me think again. In the first year, the committee was H, F, V, Z. So, in the second year, the chairman must be one of F, V, Z.\n\nBut the options are F, G, Y, I. So, only F is possible.\n\nTherefore, the answer should be A) F.\n</think>\n\nThe correct answer is A) F.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **First Year Committee:**\n   - Chairman: H (judge)\n   - Judges: H and F (since I can't be a judge if V is a scientist)\n   - Scientists: V and Z (Y is excluded due to H being present)\n   - Constraints satisfied: G and V aren't together, H and Y aren't together, only V is present (not I).\n\n2. **Second Year Constraints:**\n   - H retires, so can't be on the committee.\n   - Chairman must be from the first year's committee: F, V, or Z.\n   - Options given: A) F, B) G, C) Y, D) I.\n\n3. **Evaluating Options:**\n   - **A) F:** Valid, as F was on the first year's committee and can chair the second year.\n   - **B) G:** Invalid, as G wasn't on the first year's committee.\n   - **C) Y:** Invalid, as Y wasn't on the first year's committee.\n   - **D) I:** Invalid, as I wasn't on the first year's committee.\n\n4. **Second Year Committee Possibility with F as Chairman:**\n   - Judges: F and I (or F and G, but I is valid as per constraints)\n   - Scientists: Y and Z (since V is excluded if I is a judge)\n   - All constraints are satisfied.\n\nThus, the only possible chairman from the given options is F.\n\n**Answer:** A) F",
