ne call.\n\nXiao Li called Xiao Zhao, so Xiao Li must have answered at least one call. Because if she hadn't answered any calls, she couldn't have made any calls. So, Xiao Li must have answered a call. But who called her? Xiao Wang called everyone, including her. So, Xiao Wang called Xiao Li, and since Xiao Li made a call, she must have answered at least one call, which could be Xiao Wang's call. So, that would mean Xiao Li answered Xiao Wang's call. So, option B might be correct.\n\nWait, but the context doesn't explicitly say that Xiao Li answered Xiao Wang's call. It just says Xiao Wang called everyone, and Xiao Li called Xiao Zhao. So, Xiao Li must have answered at least one call, but it could be someone else, not necessarily Xiao Wang. But since Xiao Wang called everyone, including Xiao Li, and Xiao Li must have answered at least one call, the only possible call she could have answered is Xiao Wang's, because no one else is mentioned as calling her. Unless someone else called her, but the context doesn't mention that. So, perhaps Xiao Li answered Xiao Wang's call.\n\nSo, option B could be correct.\n\nWait, but let me check again. The context says Xiao Wang dialed everyone, so he called Xiao Li. Xiao Li called Xiao Zhao. Now, according to point 3, since Xiao Li made a call, she must have answered at least one call. The only call she could have answered is Xiao Wang's, because no one else is mentioned as calling her. So, she must have answered Xiao Wang's call. Therefore, option B is correct.\n\nWait, but earlier I thought option C might not be correct, but let me check again. Option C says someone called Xiao Wang. But the context doesn't mention anyone calling Xiao Wang. So, unless someone did, we can't infer that. So, option C is not necessarily correct.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the correct answer is B.\n</think>\n\nThe correct answer is B) Xiao Li once answered a phone call from Xiao Wang.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Understanding the Context:**\n   - Xiao Wang called everyone in the department.\n   - Xiao Li called Xiao Zhao, but Xiao Zhao didn't call anyone else.\n   - Those who never answered calls haven't made any calls.\n\n2. **Analyzing Each Option:**\n   - **Option A:** Xiao Zhao might have answered Xiao Li's call; we don't know for sure.\n   - **Option B:** Xiao Li must have answered at least one call (since she made a call). The only call she could have answered is Xiao Wang's, as he called everyone.\n   - **Option C:** There's no information that someone called Xiao Wang.\n   - **Option D:** Xiao Wang called everyone, but there's no info he answered all calls.\n\n3. **Conclusion:**\n   - Option B is the only inference supported by the given information.\n\n**Answer:** B) Xiao Li once answered a phone call from Xiao Wang.",
