      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I have this logical reasoning problem to solve. Let me read through the context and the question carefully. \n\nThe context talks about the emergence of modern science and mentions that the prosperity of Puritanism is an important external reason. It says that a prerequisite hypothesis of modern science is a widespread belief in the order of things, especially nature. Then it gives some specific data: seven out of ten members of the Royal Society in the 17th century were Puritans, which is higher than their proportion in the general population. It also mentions that many scientists were active teachers, and Puritan schools included natural science subjects in their curriculum.\n\nThe question is asking what the text is intended to illustrate, with options A to D.\n\nLet me break down each option:\n\nA) The reason why Puritanism prevailed in the 17th century. Hmm, the context does mention that Puritanism was prosperous, but it's more about how that prosperity influenced science rather than explaining why Puritanism itself was prevalent. So maybe not A.\n\nB) There is no absolute opposition between religion and science. The text does show a connection between Puritanism and science, but it doesn't explicitly state that there's no opposition. It just shows a positive influence, so B might be a possible answer, but I'm not sure if it's the main point.\n\nC) Religion has an inducing and promoting effect on modern science. This seems to fit because the context is discussing how Puritanism (a religion) contributed to the development of modern science by fostering beliefs in order, supporting scientists, and including science in education.\n\nD) The premise hypothesis of modern science and the origin of religion. The context does talk about the premise hypothesis (belief in order) but doesn't discuss the origin of religion. So D seems off-topic.\n\nSo, putting it together, the text is illustrating how Puritanism, as a religious movement, had a promoting effect on modern science. Therefore, the correct answer should be C.\n</think>\n\nThe text discusses how Puritanism influenced the development of modern science by fostering beliefs in the order of nature, supporting scientists, and integrating science into education. This indicates that religion played a promoting role in the emergence of modern science.\n\n**Answer: C) Religion has an inducing and promoting effect on modern science**",
