 responsibility isn't just on the enterprises but also on others in the chain, like the behind-the-scenes people, local departments, and equipment manufacturers. So the intended statement is about the entire chain being responsible, not just the companies.\n\nOption C says that to end the fraud, the whole chain must be addressed. That seems to be the main point. Option B is also about not just punishing the companies, but it's more about punishment, whereas the context is more about responsibility and the chain of interests.\n\nSo I think the correct answer is C.\n</think>\n\nThe context emphasizes that environmental data fraud involves a chain of interests, implicating not just the enterprises but also behind-the-scenes actors, local departments, and equipment manufacturers. The intended statement is about addressing the entire chain to end the fraud.\n\n**Answer: C) To put an end to environmental data fraud must be the whole chain**",
