ment problem of a large number of migrants is a potential crisis in urbanized areas.\n- The context does mention unemployment as a problem, but it's a consequence of the low quality of the floating population. The main point is more about the overall issue with the floating population's quality, not just unemployment. So D might be a supporting point rather than the main one.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the main point is that having a large number of low-quality floating population is bad for urbanization. Therefore, the answer should be C.\n</think>\n\nThe main point of the context is that the presence of a large number of low-quality floating population hinders urbanization. \n\nAnswer: C) The existence of a large number of low-quality floating population is not conducive to the development of urbanization.",
