 people, if J is on day 3, then G must be on day 3 with J, because O is already on day 3. So, day 3 would be O and J, and G would have to be on day 3 with J, but that would make three people on day 3, which isn't allowed. Therefore, J cannot be on day 3 because that would require G to be on day 3 as well, making three people. So, case 2 is invalid.\n\nTherefore, the only possible cases are:\n\nCase 1: H on day 1, J on day 2.\n\nCase 3: H on day 3, J on day 4.\n\nBut wait, day 3 has O, so if H is on day 3, J would be on day 4. That's possible.\n\nSo, let's consider both cases.\n\nFirst, let's consider Case 1: H on day 1, J on day 2.\n\nSo, day 1: H and someone else.\n\nDay 2: J and someone else.\n\nDay 3: O and someone else.\n\nDay 4: L and someone else, since L is on day 4 and another day (either day 1 or 2).\n\nBut L is on two days, so L is on day 4 and either day 1 or 2.\n\nLet's see.\n\nIf L is on day 4 and day 1, then day 1 would be H and L.\n\nThen, day 2 would be J and someone else.\n\nBut condition (3): G must be on the same day as J or O. So, G must be on day 2 with J or on day 3 with O.\n\nIf G is on day 2 with J, then day 2 is J and G.\n\nIf G is on day 3 with O, then day 3 is O and G.\n\nBut let's see.\n\nIf day 1 is H and L, day 2 is J and G, day 3 is O and someone else, day 4 is L and someone else.\n\nBut we have to assign all seven people, each on one or two days.\n\nWait, the people are G, H, J, K, L, M, O.\n\nSo, each day has two people, four days, so 8 slots, but one person is on two days, so total people used are 7, which fits.\n\nSo, let's try to assign.\n\nCase 1: H on day 1, J on day 2.\n\nDay 1: H and L.\n\nDay 2: J and G (since G must be with J or O, and J is on day 2).\n\nDay 3: O and someone else. Let's say O and K, since K must be on day 1 or 2, but day 1 is H and L, day 2 is J and G, so K can't be on day 1 or 2. Wait, that's a problem.\n\nWait, condition (4): K must be on day 1 or 2. So, in this case, if day 1 is H and L, day 2 is J and G,