E, D, C, A, B\nComparing positions:\n1st: E vs E \u2013 same. Zhao got E correct, which is not allowed. So Option C is out.\n\nOption D: C, D, E, A, B\nZhao's prediction: E, D, C, A, B\nComparing positions:\n1st: C vs E \u2013 different\n2nd: D vs D \u2013 same. Zhao got D correct, which is not allowed. So Option D is out.\n\nSo from Zhao's conditions, only Option B is possible.\n\nNow, let's check Qian Liang's conditions. He got two athletes in the correct position and two adjacent pairs correct.\n\nQian's prediction: A, E, B, C, D\n\nOption B: B, A, E, C, D\n\nComparing positions:\n1st: B vs A \u2013 different\n2nd: A vs E \u2013 different\n3rd: E vs B \u2013 different\n4th: C vs C \u2013 same. So Qian got C correct.\n5th: D vs D \u2013 same. So Qian got D correct. That's two correct positions (C and D). Good.\n\nNow check adjacent pairs in Qian's prediction: A-E, E-B, B-C, C-D.\n\nIn Option B, the pairs are B-A, A-E, E-C, C-D.\n\nLooking for matches:\nA-E: Yes, in position 2-3 of Option B, it's A-E. So that's one correct pair.\nC-D: Yes, in position 4-5 of Option B, it's C-D. So that's another correct pair.\n\nSo Qian got two correct positions (C and D) and two correct adjacent pairs (A-E and C-D). That fits the condition.\n\nWait, but let me double-check. Qian's prediction is A, E, B, C, D. So the pairs are A-E, E-B, B-C, C-D.\n\nIn Option B, the pairs are B-A, A-E, E-C, C-D.\n\nSo the correct pairs are A-E and C-D. That's two pairs. So yes, Qian got two correct positions and two correct adjacent pairs.\n\nTherefore, Option B satisfies both Zhao's and Qian's conditions.\n</think>\n\nThe correct ranking is B) B, A, E, C, D.\n\n**Answer: B**",
