      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I need to figure out the gist of the passage provided. Let me read through it again to make sure I understand the main points.\n\nThe passage starts by comparing Darwin's discovery of the law of organic development to Marx's discovery of the law of human history. It mentions that Marx's law is a simple fact hidden by complicated ideologies. The key idea here is that people must first take care of their basic needs\u2014eating, drinking, living, and clothing\u2014before they can engage in higher pursuits like politics, science, art, or religion. \n\nSo, the passage is emphasizing that the production of material means of livelihood is the foundation upon which other aspects of society, like national systems, legal viewpoints, art, and religious ideas, are built. It's saying that these higher aspects can't be properly understood without looking at the economic base first.\n\nLooking at the options:\n\nA) Talks about Darwin's discovery and its significance. But the passage is more focused on Marx's law, so A might not be the main gist.\n\nB) This option mentions Marx's discovery and its significance. That seems relevant because the passage does discuss Marx's law and its importance.\n\nC) States that the production of direct material means is the foundation. This is a key point from the passage, but is it the gist or just a part of it?\n\nD) Says that people's national system, legal point of view, etc., must be explained on this basis. This is also a point from the passage but seems more like a consequence rather than the main gist.\n\nThe passage is primarily about Marx's discovery that the economic base (material production) determines the superstructure (society's institutions and ideas). So, the gist is about Marx's law and its significance, which is option B. Option C is a part of that law but doesn't capture the entire significance. Option D is a result of the law but not the main point. Option A is about Darwin, which is just a comparison in the passage, not the main focus.\n\nSo, I think the correct answer is B.\n</think>\n\nThe passage primarily discusses Marx's discovery of the law of human history, emphasizing that the production of material means of livelihood forms the foundation of societal structures. This makes option B the correct answer as it encapsulates the main idea and its significance.\n\n**Answer: B) The law of the development of human history discovered by Marx and its significance.**",
