g rufen and he zhilian\n\nWait, so the options are pairs of two people, but they could be girls or boys. So the question is, if Tang is selected, which two must be selected. So the two could be girls or boys.\n\nBut from the girls' side, since Guo can't be selected, the two girls must be Fang and He. So in the group, Fang and He are definitely selected.\n\nSo looking at the options, D is Fang and He, which are the two girls. So D must be selected.\n\nBut let me check the boys as well. Since the boys have to be Tang plus two others, but with the constraints.\n\nWait, but the question is about which two must be selected, not necessarily the girls. So perhaps the answer is D, because the two girls must be Fang and He.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the answer is C, which includes Peng and He. But He is a girl, so that's mixing.\n\nWait, no, the options are pairs, but the question is about the group of five, which includes both girls and boys. So the two that must be selected could be any two, regardless of gender.\n\nBut let's think again. If Tang is selected, then:\n\nGirls: Must be Fang and He, because Guo is excluded.\n\nBoys: Tang is selected, and we need two more from Peng, Ren, Song, but with the constraints that Peng and Song can't be together, and Qiu is excluded.\n\nSo the boys could be Tang, Peng, Ren or Tang, Song, Ren.\n\nSo in both cases, Ren is selected. So Ren must be selected.\n\nWait, but the options don't include Ren. The options are:\n\nA) Fang and Guo\n\nB) Guo and He\n\nC) Peng and He\n\nD) Fang and He\n\nSo the only option that includes two girls that must be selected is D: Fang and He.\n\nBut wait, the question is asking which two must be selected, not necessarily the girls. So perhaps the answer is D because the two girls must be Fang and He.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the answer is C, but that includes He, a girl, and Peng, a boy. But is Peng necessarily selected?\n\nWait, no. Because the boys could be Tang, Song, and Ren, so Peng might not be selected. 