      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I need to figure out which option best summarizes the given paragraph. Let me read through the context again to make sure I understand it properly.\n\nThe context talks about how journalism has become more assembly-line due to professionalism, and the step-by-step framework of news production hides the necessity and importance of certain principles. But then, the earthquake has revived the moral requirements in news reports. It clarifies that this morality isn't just about simple right and wrong judgments or following professional ethics, but also includes extensive humanistic care and the courage behind that care.\n\nSo the main points are:\n1. Journalism has become too formulaic, losing some important principles.\n2. The earthquake brought back the need for moral requirements in news.\n3. These moral requirements are broader than just ethics; they include humanistic care and courage.\n\nNow, looking at the options:\n\nA) The earthquake once again awakened the moral demands of long-neglected news reports.\n- This seems to capture that the earthquake revived moral demands, but it doesn't mention the broader aspects like humanistic care and courage.\n\nB) News reporting needs to have moral requirements.\n- This is a general statement but doesn't specify what those requirements include, which the context does.\n\nC) The moral requirements of news reporting include not only professional ethics, but also humanistic care and courage.\n- This directly mentions the components of the moral requirements as discussed in the context.\n\nD) Journalists should report the earthquake in accordance with the requirements of journalistic ethics.\n- This is too specific to the earthquake and doesn't address the broader moral aspects mentioned.\n\nSo, option C seems to best summarize the paragraph because it includes all the key elements: professional ethics, humanistic care, and courage. The other options either don't cover all aspects or are too vague