      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I have this logical reasoning problem to solve. Let me try to break it down step by step. \n\nFirst, the context is about whether we should charge people for rescue operations when they go on intentional adventures that require public resources. There are two sides: the positive side thinks we should charge, and the opposite side thinks we shouldn't.\n\nThe question is asking which of the options, if true, cannot support the positive side's viewpoint. So, I need to find the option that goes against the idea of charging for rescues.\n\nLet me look at each option one by one.\n\nOption A: \"A rational citizen should be responsible for his own actions; otherwise, it will be unfair to other taxpayers.\" Hmm, this seems to support the positive side because it's saying that if someone takes risks, they should be responsible, and charging them would be fair to others who pay taxes. So A supports the positive side.\n\nOption B: \"The establishment of a professional rescue system requires a certain amount of financial support.\" This is talking about the need for funds to have a rescue system. If we charge for rescues, it could provide that financial support. So B also supports the positive side.\n\nOption C: \"It is the duty of government departments to rescue people in distress. Simple charges can not help adventurers build up a sense of social responsibility.\" Wait, this is saying that the government should rescue people as part of their duty, and charging a fee won't help adventurers take responsibility. So this seems to argue against charging, which would support the opposite side. Therefore, C cannot support the positive side.\n\nOption D: \"Tourist explorers who illegally enter unsafe areas and waste social resources and taxpayers' money should bear the corresponding expenses.\" This directly supports charging because it says those who misuse resources should pay. So D is on the positive side.\n\nSo, the question is asking which option cannot support the positive side. That would be option C because it argues against charging, supporting the opposite viewpoint instead.\n</think>\n\nThe correct answer is:\n\n**C) It is the duty of government departments to rescue people in distress. Simple charges can not help adventurers build up a sense of social responsibility.**\n\n**Explanation:**\nOption C supports the opposite viewpoint by emphasizing the government's duty to rescue without charging, thus not supporting the positive side's argument for charging.",
