he conclusion says that image thinking helps make major breakthroughs, and Nobel winners use it more. So the argument must assume that Nobel winners have indeed made major breakthroughs because that's why they're using image thinking. So C seems like a possible assumption because without that, the link wouldn't hold.\n\nD) Nobel prize winners are smarter and work harder than ordinary scientists. The context doesn't mention anything about being smarter or working harder. It's about the method of thinking. So D is probably not the assumption.\n\nSo, the conclusion is that image thinking leads to breakthroughs, and Nobel winners use it more. Therefore, the assumption must be that Nobel winners have made breakthroughs because that's the basis for the conclusion. Without assuming that they've made breakthroughs, the argument wouldn't hold. So the correct answer is C.\n</think>\n\nThe conclusion is based on the assumption that Nobel Prize winners have made major scientific breakthroughs, as this is necessary to link their use of image thinking to achieving those breakthroughs.\n\n**Answer: C**",
