ption C says \"as long as they are efficient and low toxicity,\" which are two of the three criteria. The context requires all three. So perhaps C is incorrect because it's missing the low residue part. Therefore, only B is correct.\n\nWait, but the context says \"chemical pesticides with high efficiency, low toxicity and low residue.\" So the option C says \"as long as they are efficient and low toxicity,\" which are two of the three. So the option is missing the low residue part. Therefore, C is incorrect because it doesn't include all the necessary criteria.\n\nSo, only B is correct.\n\nWait, but the context says \"chemical pesticides with high efficiency, low toxicity and low residue.\" So the option C says \"as long as they are efficient and low toxicity,\" which are two of the three. So the option is missing the low residue part. Therefore, C is incorrect because it's not including all the necessary conditions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.\n</think>\n\nThe correct answer is B) Agricultural antibiotics are allowed.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Understanding the Context:**\n   - Pollution-free vegetables use biological control measures (e.g., microbial pesticides, agricultural antibiotics) and chemical pesticides that are high efficiency, low toxicity, and low residue.\n\n2. **Analyzing Each Option:**\n   - **A)** Incorrect. The context uses \"such as,\" indicating examples, not requirements.\n   - **B)** Correct. Agricultural antibiotics are explicitly mentioned as allowed.\n   - **C)** Incorrect. The context requires chemical pesticides to be efficient, low toxicity, and low residue. The option omits \"low residue.\"\n   - **D)** Incorrect. The context implies safety but doesn't guarantee \"never hurt.\"\n\n3. **Conclusion:**\n   - Only option B correctly reflects the context.\n\n**Answer:** B) Agricultural antibiotics are allowed.",
