ient sages.\n- Sublating means overcoming and preserving. The text doesn't talk about preserving their thoughts but rather being inspired by their questioning and subversive nature.\n\nD) Ancient philosophical thoughts have provided assistance for scientific and innovative research.\n- The text emphasizes the sages' fundamental questions and subversive approach as a source of inspiration, which aligns with providing assistance through their thoughts.\n\nWait, but option A says their understanding is enlightening. The text says their understanding was naive, so maybe A isn't correct. Option D talks about their philosophical thoughts assisting research, which fits because the sages' questions and discussions are a form of philosophical thought that inspires scientists.\n\nAlternatively, option C mentions sublating, which might not be the right term here. The text doesn't talk about building on their thoughts but rather being inspired by their approach.\n\nSo, the purpose is to show that ancient sages, despite their naive understanding, asked fundamental questions that can inspire contemporary scientists to think outside the box. Therefore, their philosophical thoughts have provided assistance for scientific research.\n\nI think the answer is D.\n</think>\n\nThe purpose of the text is to highlight how ancient sages, through their fundamental questions and subversive approach, have provided philosophical thoughts that assist contemporary scientific and innovative research. \n\n**Answer: D**",
