nts, which violates the condition that only one is correct. So Option B is also out.\n\nOption C: Shanbei is the champion.\n\nLet's check each statement:\n\n1. Champion is Shannan or Jiangbei. Shanbei isn't either, so this is false.\n2. Champion is neither Shanbei nor Jiangnan. But the champion is Shanbei, so this statement is false.\n3. Champion is Jiangnan. That's false.\n4. Champion is not Shannan. Since the champion is Shanbei, this is true.\n\nSo only statement 4 is true. That means only one statement is correct, which fits the condition. Hmm, that seems promising. But let me check the last option just to be sure.\n\nOption D: Jiangbei is the champion.\n\nChecking each statement:\n\n1. Champion is Shannan or Jiangbei. Since Jiangbei is the champion, this is true.\n2. Champion is neither Shanbei nor Jiangnan. Jiangbei isn't either, so this is true.\n3. Champion is Jiangnan. That's false.\n4. Champion is not Shannan. Since the champion is Jiangbei, this is true.\n\nWait, so statements 1, 2, and 4 are all true. That's three correct statements, which is way more than one. So Option D is definitely out.\n\nWait, but when I checked Option C, Shanbei, only statement 4 was true. That fits the condition. So the champion must be Shanbei, which is option C.\n\nBut wait, let me double-check because sometimes I might make a mistake.\n\nIf the champion is Shanbei:\n\n1. Shannan or Jiangbei? No, so false.\n2. Neither Shanbei nor Jiangnan? But the champion is Shanbei, so this statement is false because it's saying the champion isn't Shanbei, which is incorrect.\n3. Jiangnan? No, so false.\n4. Not Shannan? Yes, because it's Shanbei, so true.\n\nYes, only statement 4 is correct. So that's the one.\n\nWait, but the options given are A, B, C, D, and the options are A) Shannan, B) Jiangnan, C) Shanbei, D) Jiangbei. So the correct answer should be C) Shanbei.\n\nBut wait, the initial problem says there are five teams, but the options only include four. Maybe the fifth team isn't relevant because the champion must be one of the four options. So yes, C is the correct answer.\n</think>\n\nThe correct answer is C) Shanbei.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **List the Statements:**\n   - (1) Champion is Shannan or Jiangbei.\n   - (2) Champion is neither Shanbei nor Jiangnan.\n   - (3) Champion is Jiangnan.\n   - (4) Champion is not Shannan.\n\n2. **Assume Each Option and Check Statements:**\n   - **Option A (Shannan):** Statements 1 and 2 are true. (Incorrect as two statements are true.)\n   - **Option B (Jiangnan):** Statements 3 and 4 are true. (Incorrect as two statements are true.)\n   - **Option C (Shanbei):** Only statement 4 is true. (Correct as only one statement is true.)\n   - **Option D (Jiangbei):** Statements 1, 2, and 4 are true. (Incorrect as three statements are true.)\n\n3. **Conclusion:** Only when Shanbei is the champion does only one statement (statement 4) hold true.\n\n**Answer:** C) Shanbei.",
