      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I need to figure out the main content of the passage provided. Let me read through it again to make sure I understand all the details.\n\nThe passage talks about the current income tax rates for domestic and foreign-funded enterprises. It mentions that the standard rate is 33%, but there are preferential rates: 24% and 15% for some foreign-funded enterprises, and 27% for domestic low-profit ones. Then, it says that the draft law proposes setting the tax rate at 25%. The reasons given for this change are to reduce the tax burden on domestic enterprises, control the fiscal revenue reduction, and consider international tax rates, especially those of neighboring countries. It also states that the average tax rate among 159 countries is 28.6%, and for 18 neighboring regions, it's 26.7%. The new 25% rate is described as moderately low internationally, which should help improve enterprise competitiveness and attract foreign investment.\n\nNow, the question is asking which option is the main content of the passage. The options are A, B, C, D.\n\nLet me break down each option:\n\nA) New measures of tax rate: from internal and external differences to equal treatment.\n- The passage does talk about different rates for domestic and foreign-funded enterprises, and the new rate aims to set a single rate of 25%. So this seems to touch on equalizing the tax treatment.\n\nB) A new starting point for enterprises: competition on the same stage and fair competition.\n- This seems related to the idea of equal treatment, as a single tax rate would put all enterprises on the same footing, promoting fair competition.\n\nC) The tax rate of 25% is moderately low internationally.\n- The passage does mention that 25% is moderately low compared to international averages, but is this the main point? It's a supporting detail rather than the main content.\n\nD) Adjusting the tax rate will help to improve the competitiveness of enterprises.\n- This is another supporting point. The passage mentions that the new rate is good for competitiveness and attracting investment, but again, it's a reason for the change, not the main content.\n\nSo, the main content is about the change in tax rates. The passage starts by explaining the current rates, then introduces the new 25% rate, and the reasons behind it. The key point is the shift from different rates for domestic and foreign to a single rate, which is a new measure. So, option A seems to capture that.\n\nOption B is about competition, which is a result of the tax change, but not the main content. Option C is a fact about the rate, and D is a benefit of the change. The main focus is on the tax rate adjustment itself, moving towards equal treatment.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer should be A.\n</think>\n\nThe main content of the passage is the introduction of a new tax rate policy that aims to equalize treatment between domestic and foreign-funded enterprises by setting a single rate of 25%. This change is intended to reduce the tax burden on domestic enterprises, control fiscal revenue reduction, and align with international standards, particularly those of neighboring countries. The passage highlights the shift from varying rates to a unified rate, emphasizing equal treatment.\n\n**Answer: A) New measures of tax rate: from internal and external differences to equal treatment.**",
