fe. Option C suggests viewing courses rationally, which is also possible, but the context already mentions that EQ is best developed in daily life, so maybe the next point is about how parents should practice it at home. Option D is about improving parents' EQ, which is related but perhaps a step further. Option A is about parents paying attention to tutoring, but the context already says that EQ classes are popular, so maybe the next point is about the actual practice rather than just attention.\n\nSo I think the next point would be about how parents should practice EQ in their family education, which is option B.\n</think>\n\nThe context emphasizes the crucial role of parents in developing children's emotional intelligence through daily life rather than just training courses. The next logical point would discuss how parents should practice this in their family education.\n\n**Answer: B) Parents' practice in family education**",
