t.\n\nLet me double-check. Prevention costs are about preventing defects before production, so things like quality control, training, design reviews. Advertising is more about selling the product, not preventing defects. So D is likely the correct answer because it's not a prevention cost.\n</think>\n\nThe correct answer is D. Advertising costs are not prevention costs as they relate to marketing rather than defect prevention.\n\n**Answer: D**",
